<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.4 pct in November - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.4 pct in November - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.79 billion zlotys, or 1.4 percent, in November to 127.88 billion after a 2.2 percent rise in October, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 22.7 percent in the January-November period against 28.9 percent in the same period of last year.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  NOVEMBER  OCTOBER	 NOV 95</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	     1.4     2.2	     2.2</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		  127.88  126.09(126.04) 99.62</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)     22.88   22.52(22.51)  20.94</p>
<p>  National currency		    105.00  103.57(103.53) 78.68</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		   23.72   23.51	   19.14</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector   76.94   73.42(73.41)  55.38</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
